## Usage

### Trigger and Inline
`inline` renders the panel directly, and `sections` limits the sections it offers.
:::TuffDemoWrapper{demo="IconPickerIconPickerDemo" code-lang="vue"}
---
code: |
  <script setup lang="ts">
  import type { IconPickerShape } from '@talex-touch/tuffex/icon-picker'
  import { TxIconPicker } from '@talex-touch/tuffex/icon-picker'
  import { ref } from 'vue'

  const identifier = ref('emoji:🚀')
  const shape = ref<IconPickerShape>('rounded')
  </script>

  <template>
    <TxIconPicker v-model="identifier" v-model:shape="shape" shape-selectable />
    <TxIconPicker v-model="identifier" inline :sections="['ai', 'icon', 'brand']" />
  </template>
---
:::

### Best Practices

- Store the identifier as-is and resolve it at render time with `parseIconIdentifier`; don't split it into two columns that can disagree.
- In modules that only read a stored value, import `parseIconIdentifier` from `@talex-touch/tuffex/icon-picker` without loading the panel.
- When narrowing `sections`, keep `ai` if users pick model vendors: vendor marks and AI glyphs live there, not under Brands or Icons.
- Turn `shapeSelectable` off when the host draws its own plate, or users pick a shape they never see.
- Use `TxIconChip` to display a small icon plate; this component only chooses one.

## API Reference

### Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|------|
| `modelValue` | `string` | `''` | The icon identifier, bound with `v-model`. |
| `shape` | `IconPickerShape` | `'rounded'` | Plate shape, bound with `v-model:shape`; `ICON_PICKER_SHAPES` lists all twelve. |
| `sections` | `IconPickerSection[]` | all five | Sections to offer, in tab order: `emoji`, `icon`, `brand`, `ai`, and `file` as a choose-file button. |
| `catalog` | `Partial<Record<IconPickerCatalogSection, IconPickerEntry[]>>` | - | Replaces a section's bundled rows; an entry's `category` groups it under a heading. |
| `shapeSelectable` | `boolean` | `true` | Shows the shape row; turn off when the host draws its own plate. |
| `fileChooser` | `() => Promise<string \| null>` | - | Host file dialog resolving to an absolute path, or `null` on cancel. |
| `accept` | `string` | `'image/*'` | Accept list for the file dialog and the fallback input. |
| `disabled` | `boolean` | `false` | Disables the trigger and the panel. |
| `size` | `number` | `44` | Edge length of the trigger plate, in px. |
| `placeholder` | `string` | `''` | The trigger's `aria-label`; falls back to the search label. |
| `inline` | `boolean` | `false` | Renders the panel directly instead of behind a trigger. |
| `labels` | `Partial<IconPickerLabels>` | English defaults | Section, shape and category names, the search placeholder, and the actions. |

### Events

| Event | Payload | Description |
|-------|---------|------|
| `update:modelValue` | `string` | Fires on a pick, with `''` when cleared. |
| `update:shape` | `IconPickerShape` | Fires when the shape changes. |
| `change` | `string` | Fires together with `update:modelValue`. |
| `file-error` | `unknown` | Fires when the chooser throws or the fallback input can't read the file. |

### Exposed Methods

| Name | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `toggle(value?)` | `(value?: boolean) => void` | Opens or closes the panel per `value`, or flips it when omitted; an `inline` panel always shows. |

## The Identifier

A pick is a `<type>:<value>` string. It splits at the *first* colon, so a value may contain colons (`url:`, a Windows `file:C:/…`).

```
emoji:🚀
class:i-ri-rocket-line
file:/Users/me/a.png
url:https://example.com/y.svg
builtin:star
```

`parseIconIdentifier` and `formatIconIdentifier` convert both ways. An unprefixed string is not guessed at and returns `null`; a bare emoji is the one exception.

```ts
import { parseIconIdentifier } from '@talex-touch/tuffex/icon-picker'

parseIconIdentifier('class:i-ri-rocket-line') // { type: 'class', value: 'i-ri-rocket-line' }
parseIconIdentifier('rocket.png')             // null
parseIconIdentifier('🚀')                      // { type: 'emoji', value: '🚀' }
```

## Rendering a Picked Class

The picker draws its bundled classes from path data it ships, so its grid needs no icon CSS from the host. Outside the picker a picked `class:` value is only a class name: give `TxIcon` the picker's glyphs through `classGlyph`, or safelist `ICON_CATALOG_CLASSES` in the host's utility-CSS engine.

```ts
import { TX_ICON_CONFIG_KEY } from '@talex-touch/tuffex'
import { resolveIconPickerGlyph } from '@talex-touch/tuffex/icon-picker'

app.provide(TX_ICON_CONFIG_KEY, { classGlyph: resolveIconPickerGlyph })
```

```ts
import { ICON_CATALOG_CLASSES } from '@talex-touch/tuffex/icon-picker'

export default defineConfig({
  safelist: [...ICON_CATALOG_CLASSES],
})
```

## Overview

- Search covers every section at once, the open tab first. It matches keywords, class names and category headings, tolerates a typo, and takes Chinese, full pinyin or initials (`火箭`, `huojian`, `hj`).
- Focus stays in the search box: arrow keys move through the grid, Enter picks the highlighted cell (the top result while searching), and Esc clears the query before it closes the panel.
- Browsing groups a section by category, with a row of shortcuts that jumps between them.
- The trigger morphs from one plate outline to the next; under reduced motion it switches at once.
- The file section depends on the host: pass `fileChooser` (for example an Electron `dialog.showOpenDialog` bridge); without it, a hidden `<input type="file">` yields a data URL.
- `shape` is presentational and stored separately; it is not part of the identifier.

## Technologies

- Glyph path data is generated by `scripts/generate-icon-picker-data.mjs` and loaded per section the first time it is shown; the plate morphs through TxIconMorph's engine.
- Remix Icon 4.8.0 data ships under Apache-2.0 (`REMIXICON-LICENSE`) and Simple Icons data under CC0-1.0; brand marks remain trademarks of their owners.
- Source: `packages/tuffex/packages/components/src/icon-picker/`.

